{
 "schema": "mnbl.naval-content",
 "version": 1,
 "notes": "MMR-35 generated ports, fleets and naval faction records (docs/naval-content.md). Owner: NavalContentFactory (src/MNBL.ProceduralWorld/Campaign/NavalContentFactory.cs). Every value comes from the installed campaign and the installed War Sails campaign map scene; no Calradia coordinate or settlement id is carried into a generated world. Scene entities (port markers, blockade arcs, village drop-offs, pirate spawn points) are intents for MMR-40, which places the map entities.",
 "streams": {
  "rule": "value(stream, version, world prefix, entity, draw) = first 8 bytes of sha256(\"mnbl.naval-stream/1\\n\" + stream + \"\\n\" + version + \"\\n\" + prefix + \"\\n\" + entity + \"\\n\" + draw), big-endian; construction only",
  "pirates": 1
 },
 "water": {
  "rule": "water cells are the travel cells of class sea, lake or river (cells.bin), joined by shared edges with columns wrapping; a water component takes the MMR-28 basin id of the port and coast transitions on it; a component is open when it holds a sea cell and at least minOpenCells cells (the MMR-28 rule). A sea cell is open sea when every cell within openSeaCells (Chebyshev) is sea",
  "minOpenCells": 16,
  "openSeaCells": 4,
  "playabilitySha256": "6269c9db66e9a52f514d5bc78a1552b552d2e17899038d184663118b3957e54d"
 },
 "shipyards": {
  "rule": "every port town on an open basin gets building_shipyard (BuildingsCampaignBehavior adds it at game start for IsTown && HasPort anyway, at its start level 1, and CanTownCreateShipFromHull dereferences it); its level follows the installed port towns' shares, assigned in order of the port's harbour quality (the MMR-28 chosen candidate), best first: the top share level 3, then 2, the rest 1. The 3 installed port towns without a shipyard in XML count at level 1, the level the game gives them at start (town_A7, town_S2, town_V7)",
