 "fleets": {
  "rule": "a clan may hold ships only when its home settlement's land group holds a port town on an open basin (its parties can reach an anchor). The installed ShipTradeCampaignBehavior buys ships for a clan with a fixed chance (0.5 a day, and at the new game's follow-ups) from its map faction's fiefs, else 20% of the time from any non-hostile town, for a party ShipDistributionModel.CanPartyTakeShip accepts, with no reachability check; it sells when the clan holds more than ClanShipOwnershipModel.GetIdealShipNumberForClan. The generated ShipDistributionModel refuses ships to the parties of a clan without a reachable port (and fleet transfers to them), and the generated ClanShipOwnershipModel gives such a clan an ideal fleet of 0, so any ship it still holds is sold; both delegate every other clan to the installed models. A kingdom is coastal when one of its towns is such a port town, else landlocked (named reason). Initial ships come from the installed path: ShipProductionCampaignBehavior builds them at shipyards and ShipTradeCampaignBehavior sells them to clan parties (ChangeShipOwnerAction), during the new game's follow-ups"
 },
